codex
Two serious gaps remain in section 4.

1. **A written result does not prove the run completed.** The [state table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-25-grouping-acceptance.md:65) maps “已写结果” to `complete`. But the runner [writes the result before checking history and resend](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/hierarchy_study/subject_names.py:203), and can subsequently record failure. A crash can also leave a result with missing or failed `checks.json`. Unchanging file hashes do not resolve this. The table needs explicit outcomes for these combinations, including failure precedence and which completion records are required. Otherwise a stable, unfinished snapshot can appear complete.

2. **The nonempty old-format path has no planned test.** The [contract requires reading old-format references](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-25-grouping-acceptance.md:67), but the [verification table](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-10-25-grouping-acceptance.md:83) supplies empty originals and a nonempty fixture rewritten into names. The saved [old-format control has no candidates or declarations](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/reports/2026-10-25-subject-names-01/sample-dev-1-control/item3-extract.json:213). Consequently, every listed test could pass while nonempty old-format checking is broken. Add a nonempty old-format positive control and corresponding wrong/missing-reference counterexamples through the checker entry point.

These are checker-design findings. Reporting semantics as pending is appropriate. No files were edited or models called.
